- action(n1, "Start the booking process"): This action is hallucinated; the source text specifies that to begin with, you should "choose your destination and calculate the distance".
- precedence(n2, n3): The model strictly sequences choosing the destination (n2) and checking the need to book a flight (n3), which violates the concurrency explicitly stated in the source text ("While doing so, continue to check...").
- guard(b3, n14, v3 = 'No') and action(n14, "Process ends"): The model hallucinates a path where 24 hours have not passed leading to the process ending. The source text only specifies what to do "if 24 hours have passed" as the exhaustive "Otherwise" condition.